d physical and environmental security model. \\nSoftware \\nAdobe Management has a focus on scaling software solutions to efficiently support Adobe’s Experience Cloud \\noperational environment. The following key systems and applications are leveraged to support Adobe’s Experience \\nCloud core solutions: \\nApplication \\nDescription \\nChange Management \\nGitHub Enterprise \\nGitHub is a centralized source code control system. It is implemented internally for the \\nmanagement of code repositories. \\nGitLab \\n(Workfront only) GitLab is a source code management platform for Git repositories, as well \\nas a code deployment tool used for production environments \\nService Knowledge \\nManagement System \\n(SKMS) \\nSKMS is an internally developed set of tools, information, and systems that govern change \\nand support Adobe technical operations.  \\nJenkins \\nJenkins is an open-source continuous integration tool for dissemination of builds and \\nchange management controls for the production environment. Je", "confidence_justification": ["+0.4: in common subservice orgs list", "+0.1: likely_so is Yes", "+0.1: common_so is Yes", "GPT-4o review failed: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0) | Response: \'```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\"is_likely_subservice_org\\": true,\\\\n  \\"reason\\": \\"GitHub is a centralized source code control system that many organizations use to manage and store their source code. In the context of SOC 2 compliance, if an organization relies on GitHub for critical aspects of its operations, such as version control and collaboration on code, it would likely be considered a subservice organization. This is because GitHub\\\\\'s services could impact the organization\\\\\'s ability to meet the trust service criteria related to security, availability, and confidentiality.\\"\\\\n}\\\\n```\'"]}, {"third_party_name": "GitLab", "third_party_description": "Source code management platform for Git repositories and code deployment tool", "third_party_pa