s (AWS) provides infrastructure as a service, which is commonly used by organizations to host their applications and data. In a SOC 2 report, AWS would likely be identified as a subservice organization because it plays a critical role in the organization\\\\\'s overall control environment, particularly in areas related to security, availability, and confidentiality.\\"\\\\n}\\\\n```\'"]', '[{"third_party_control_seq": 1, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": "Policies and procedures exist to ensure that logical access to production systems is restricted to authorized personnel."}, {"third_party_control_seq": 1, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": "Policies and procedures exist to ensure that logical access to production systems is restricted to authorized personnel."}, {"third_party_control_seq": 6, "third_party_control_id": "CC6.6", "third_party_control_desc": null}]']
