2025-07-24 04:16:19,743 INFO: SQL: INSERT INTO subservice_org (name, confidence, scan_id, third_party_description, third_party_page_ref, third_party_confidence, distance_from_so_keywords, likely_so, common_so, source_context, confidence_justification, third_party_controls) VALUES (%s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING | Values: ['Google Cloud Platform', 0.9, 18, 'Google Cloud Platform is a suite of cloud computing services that runs on the same infrastructure that Google uses internally for its end-user products.', 'https://cloud.google.com/,PAGE 19,PAGE 19', 0.9, 0, 'Yes', 'Yes', 'ncluding updates and security patches), application software, and \nthe configuration of the security group firewall provided by the subservice organization. \n \nKey AWS services utilized by Adobe include: \n• Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2) \n• Simple Storage Service (S3) \n• Relational Database Service (RDS) \n• Identity Access Management (IAM) \n• Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) \n• Security Groups \n• Lambda Functions \n \nAdobe periodically reviews third-party assurance reports to verify that AWS continually \nsubscribes to a defined physical, environmental, and virtual security model. \nGoogle (Subservice \nOrganization) \n(Workfront only) Google Cloud Platform (GCP) directs and controls operations as well as \nestablishes, communicates, and monitors policies and procedures for some of the \nproduction environments for Adobe Workfront solutions. In addition, it operates, manages, \nand controls the components from the virtualization layer to the physical security of the \nfacilities in which Adobe Workfron', '["Filtered by GPT: This is a cloud provider offering a suite of cloud computing services.", "+0.4: in common subservice orgs list", "+0.1: likely_so is Yes", "+0.1: common_so is Yes", "GPT-4o review failed: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0) | Response: \'```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\"is_likely_subservice_org\\": true,\\\\n  \\"reason\\": \\"Google Cloud Platform provides infrastructure and services that organizations may rely on to deliver their own services, making it a likely subservice organization in a SOC 2 report.\\"\\\\n}\\\\n```\'"]', '[{"third_party_control_seq": 1, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}, {"third_party_control_seq": 1, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}, {"third_party_control_seq": 2, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}, {"third_party_control_seq": 3, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}]']
2025-07-24 04:16:19,744 INFO: Inserted into subservice_org: ['Google Cloud Platform', 0.9, 18, 'Google Cloud Platform is a suite of cloud computing services that runs on the same infrastructure that Google uses internally for its end-user products.', 'https://cloud.google.com/,PAGE 19,PAGE 19', 0.9, 0, 'Yes', 'Yes', 'ncluding updates and security patches), application software, and \nthe configuration of the security group firewall provided by the subservice organization. \n \nKey AWS services utilized by Adobe include: \n• Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2) \n• Simple Storage Service (S3) \n• Relational Database Service (RDS) \n• Identity Access Management (IAM) \n• Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) \n• Security Groups \n• Lambda Functions \n \nAdobe periodically reviews third-party assurance reports to verify that AWS continually \nsubscribes to a defined physical, environmental, and virtual security model. \nGoogle (Subservice \nOrganization) \n(Workfront only) Google Cloud Platform (GCP) directs and controls operations as well as \nestablishes, communicates, and monitors policies and procedures for some of the \nproduction environments for Adobe Workfront solutions. In addition, it operates, manages, \nand controls the components from the virtualization layer to the physical security of the \nfacilities in which Adobe Workfron', '["Filtered by GPT: This is a cloud provider offering a suite of cloud computing services.", "+0.4: in common subservice orgs list", "+0.1: likely_so is Yes", "+0.1: common_so is Yes", "GPT-4o review failed: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0) | Response: \'```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\"is_likely_subservice_org\\": true,\\\\n  \\"reason\\": \\"Google Cloud Platform provides infrastructure and services that organizations may rely on to deliver their own services, making it a likely subservice organization in a SOC 2 report.\\"\\\\n}\\\\n```\'"]', '[{"third_party_control_seq": 1, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}, {"third_party_control_seq": 1, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}, {"third_party_control_seq": 2, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}, {"third_party_control_seq": 3, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}]']
2025-07-24 04:16:19,744 INFO: SQL: INSERT INTO subservice_org (name, confidence, scan_id, third_party_description, third_party_page_ref, third_party_confidence, distance_from_so_keywords, likely_so, common_so, source_context, confidence_justification, third_party_controls) VALUES (%s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s, %s) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING | Values: ['GitHub', 0.9, 18, 'Centralized source code control system', 'Page 21', 0.9, 3, 'Yes', 'Yes', 'ribe to a defined physical and environmental security model. \nSoftware \nAdobe Management has a focus on scaling software solutions to efficiently support Adobe’s Experience Cloud \noperational environment. The following key systems and applications are leveraged to support Adobe’s Experience \nCloud core solutions: \nApplication \nDescription \nChange Management \nGitHub Enterprise \nGitHub is a centralized source code control system. It is implemented internally for the \nmanagement of code repositories. \nGitLab \n(Workfront only) GitLab is a source code management platform for Git repositories, as well \nas a code deployment tool used for production environments \nService Knowledge \nManagement System \n(SKMS) \nSKMS is an internally developed set of tools, information, and systems that govern change \nand support Adobe technical operations.  \nJenkins \nJenkins is an open-source continuous integration tool for dissemination of builds and \nchange management controls for the production environment. Je', '["+0.4: in common subservice orgs list", "+0.1: likely_so is Yes", "+0.1: common_so is Yes", "GPT-4o review failed: Expecting value: line 1 column 1 (char 0) | Response: \'```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\"is_likely_subservice_org\\": true,\\\\n  \\"reason\\": \\"GitHub is a centralized source code control system that many organizations use to manage and store their source code. In the context of SOC 2 compliance, if an organization relies on GitHub for critical aspects of its operations, such as version control and collaboration on code, it would likely be considered a subservice organization. This is because GitHub\\\\\'s services could impact the organization\\\\\'s ability to meet the trust service criteria related to security, availability, and confidentiality.\\"\\\\n}\\\\n```\'"]', '[{"third_party_control_seq": 1, "third_party_control_id": null, "third_party_control_desc": null}]']
